 words, SEO term in first paragraph and a `##`, then `pnpm --dir sites/koios.news run check` plus local server probes. - The 2026-06-19 source cycle showed that Search Console demand pull still returns `403` for `sc-domain:koios.news`; until permissions are fixed, farm assignments come from seed/static demand rather than live search demand. - The 2026-06-19 source cycles showed assignment/story alignment problems: the farm paired `crypto mining energy demand` with a UK re...","Prior research (src/content/assets/legacy/2026-07-03-koios.news/memory/_index.md, sha256:2fdd12ac39894400c92f8947f2adba68e10867fb1926cd0725e10d7d3d97d5a6): Until restored, use the documented rules directly: frontmatter shape, >=800 body words, SEO term in first paragraph and a `##`, then `pnpm --dir sites/koios.news run check` plus local server probes. - The 2026-06-19 source cycle showed that Search Console demand pull still returns `403` for `sc-domain:koios.news`; until permissions are fixed, farm assignments come from seed/static demand rather than live search demand. - The 2026-06-19 source cycles showed assignment/story alignment problems: the farm paired `crypto mining energy demand` with a UK retail heat story earlier, then paired `farmland and water rights` with a UK borrowing/water-shares market story. Human editing changed the lat...","Prior research (src/content/assets/legacy/2026-07-03-koios.news/memory/_index.md, sha256:2fdd12ac39894400c92f8947f2adba68e10867fb1926cd0725e10d7d3d97d5a6): - The 2026-06-19 source cycles showed assignment/story alignment problems: the farm paired `crypto mining energy demand` with a UK retail heat story earlier, then paired `farmland and water rights` with a UK borrowing/water-shares market story. Human editing changed the latter SEO term to `UK borrowing and water shares` and narrowed the copy. Source-cycle repair packets now expose this friction from run traces, and operators can convert those packets into durable editing assignments. A repair assignment now exists for `ai-capital-expenditure-bubble` after an unsupported-demand obstruction. Future writing-flow work should make research packets or claim overlap gate the assignment before dr...","Prior research (src/content/assets/legacy/2026-07-03-koios.news/memory/_index.md, sha256:2fdd12ac39894400c92f8947f2adba68e10867fb1926cd0725e10d7d3d97d5a6): A repair assignment now exists for `ai-capital-expenditure-bubble` after an unsupported-demand obstruction. Future writing-flow work should make research packets or claim overlap gate the assignment before drafting. - The escalated 2026-06-19 source cycle also exposed a slug/path collision: the farm tried to write a new `uk-bond-yields-rise-as-water-company-shares-fall` draft over a previously published article, temporarily reverting it to `draft: true` with no references. The article was restored, and the source-cycle wrapper now snapshots existing manuscripts, restores collided paths, skips post-processing for those candidates, and reports `candidateWriteCollisions`. Future upstream wor...","Prior research (content/assets/legacy/koios.news/561-group/sites/koios.news/memory/_index.md, sha256:5cebe3639dae72307cc5236a4c30c07e92690c2e26ff74a85e4667ba4338b702): - **The newsroom source model is nested** as `src/researching/sourcing` and `src/researching/writing/editing/publishing/managing/{advertising,circulating,syndicating}`. The backend reading nests the same production line: researching -> writing -> editing -> publishing -> managing. Internal planning now has `src/administrating/developing`, exposed in `/departments.json`, human board `/administrating/developing`, `/administrating/developing.json`, OpenAPI, and MCP tool `read_developing`. Its `topologyConstruction` section records the current upstream/content-derived plan for nested component topology: source-to-reference fibration, desk-chain nesting, article sheaf/cosheaf, newsroom swarm h...","Prior research (content/assets/legacy/koios.news/561-group/sites/koios.news/memory/_index.md, sha256:5cebe3639dae72307cc5236a4c30c07e92690c2e26ff74a85e4667ba4338b702): The newsroom web desk now renders the top five conservative internal-link placement packets with source/target/evidence/preview and an `Apply link` form; the form submits the same stale-safe expected paragraph witness through `/operators/content/internal-link-placements/form`. Draft-time same-site link guidance now sits before publication: `/operators/writing/internal-link-guidance.json`, `/operators/assignments/{assignmentId}/link-guidance.json`, MCP tool `read_draft_internal_link_guidance`, research-packet HTML, assignment work-order HTML, and assignment draft forms all expose published Koios article targets to consider while writing. This is composition guidance only: it excludes assig...","Prior research (content/assets/legacy/koios.news/561-group/sites/koios.news/memory/_index.md, sha256:5cebe3639dae72307cc5236a4c30c07e92690c2e26ff74a85e4667ba4338b702): `/operators/assignments/{assignmentId}/manuscripts` and MCP tool `create_assignment_draft` create a draft directly from an assigned item, promoting assignment source URLs into CSL manuscript references while carrying the assignment id, beat, and SEO term. The assignment work-order and draft form show same-site link guidance before body composition. The newsroom web CMS now exposes HTML forms for `/operators/assignments/new`, `/operators/manuscripts/new`, and `/operators/assignments/{assignmentId}/manuscripts/new`; their POST handlers reuse the same assignment/draft normalizers and write operations as the JSON API. `/operators/manuscripts.json` gives the machine manuscript inventory: draft...","Prior research (content/assets/legacy/koios.news/561-group/sites/koios.news/memory/_index.md, sha256:5cebe3639dae72307cc5236a4c30c07e92690c2e26ff74a85e4667ba4338b702): Publishing is gated by `src/researching/writing/editing/standards.mts`, which reviews canonical CSL `references:` records, body citations, body length, H2/body separation, SEO placement, license, license URL, syndication rights, and existing gate metadata before clearing a draft. Article frontmatter `sources:` is invalid at the publication layer; sources are intake material, references are the cited cut used by writing/editing. Draft creation and the repair action default to `CC BY 4.0` with `https://creativecommons.org/licenses/by/4.0/` and explicit syndication rights for indexing, snippets, large previews, feeds, Google Search/News/Discover surfaces, and attributed downstream distributi...","Prior research (content/assets/legacy/koios.news/561-group/sites/koios.news/memory/_index.md, sha256:5cebe3639dae72307cc5236a4c30c07e92690c2e26ff74a85e4667ba4338b702): `content/posts/uk-bond-yields-rise-as-water-company-shares-fall.md` (2026-06-19) was generated by `pnpm run source:cycle` from the `collapse-finance` wire, normalized from intake `sources:` to canonical CSL `references:`, enriched with source-cycle same-site link guidance, human-edited to remove unsupported speculative climate/resource claims, given a second ONS reference, published through `POST /operators/manuscripts/uk-bond-yields-rise-as-water-company-shares-fall/publish`, and redeployed. It is live on the homepage and RSS feed, has `referenceCount: 2`, `draft: false`, and no standards findings. `content/posts/world-cup-faces-air-quality-disaster-as-wildfires-threaten.md` was repaired...","Prior research (content/assets/legacy/koios.news/561-group/sites/koios.news/memory/_index.md, sha256:5cebe3639dae72307cc5236a4c30c07e92690c2e26ff74a85e4667ba4338b702): The `hello-world` article renders that A-Ads iframe from frontmatter under the fingerprint/banner image, and the public CSP/privacy policy recognize the A-Ads frame. - **The content and data stores are submodules.** Posts live in `content/posts/`; data lives in `data/`, with append-only traces under `data/logs/` and current JSON records under `data/records/`. - **The content-production instance is configured in** `content-production.config.json`: Koios's farm property, seed terms, beat sources, Search Console property, front-matter namespace, voice, gates, model, content store, and data store. `package.json` is package/site metadata, not the farm instance carrier. The seed vocabulary now...","Prior research (content/assets/legacy/koios.news/561-group/sites/koios.news/memory/_index.md, sha256:5cebe3639dae72307cc5236a4c30c07e92690c2e26ff74a85e4667ba4338b702): - The manual workshop references `scripts/new-post.mjs` and `scripts/lint-post.mjs`, but no `scripts/` directory is present in this package. Until restored, use the documented rules directly: frontmatter shape, >=800 body words, SEO term in first paragraph and a `##`, then `pnpm --dir sites/koios.news run check` plus local server probes. - The 2026-06-19 source cycle showed that Search Console demand pull still returns `403` for `sc-domain:koios.news`; until permissions are fixed, farm assignments come from seed/static demand rather than live search demand. - The 2026-06-19 source cycles showed assignment/story alignment problems: the farm paired `crypto mining energy demand` with a UK re...","Prior research (content/assets/legacy/koios.news/561-group/sites/koios.news/memory/_index.md, sha256:5cebe3639dae72307cc5236a4c30c07e92690c2e26ff74a85e4667ba4338b702): - The manual workshop references `scripts/new-post.mjs` and `scripts/lint-post.mjs`, but no `scripts/` directory is present in this package. Until restored, use the documented rules directly: frontmatter shape, >=800 body words, SEO term in first paragraph and a `##`, then `pnpm --dir sites/koios.news run check` plus local server probes. - The 2026-06-19 source cycle showed that Search Console demand pull still returns `403` for `sc-domain:koios.news`; until permissions are fixed, farm assignments come from seed/static demand rather than live search demand. - The 2026-06-19 source cycles showed assignment/story alignment problems: the farm paired `crypto mining energy demand` with a UK re...","Prior research (content/assets/legacy/koios.news/561-group/sites/koios.news/memory/_index.md, sha256:5cebe3639dae72307cc5236a4c30c07e92690c2e26ff74a85e4667ba4338b702): - The 2026-06-19 source cycle showed that Search Console demand pull still returns `403` for `sc-domain:koios.news`; until permissions are fixed, farm assignments come from seed/static demand rather than live search demand. - The 2026-06-19 source cycles showed assignment/story alignment problems: the farm paired `crypto mining energy demand` with a UK retail heat story earlier, then paired `farmland and water rights` with a UK borrowing/water-shares market story. Human editing changed the latter SEO term to `UK borrowing and water shares` and narrowed the copy. Source-cycle repair packets now expose this friction from run traces, and operators can convert those packets into durable editi...","Prior research (content/assets/legacy/koios.news/561-group/sites/koios.news/memory/_index.md, sha256:5cebe3639dae72307cc5236a4c30c07e92690c2e26ff74a85e4667ba4338b702): - The 2026-06-19 source cycles showed assignment/story alignment problems: the farm paired `crypto mining energy demand` with a UK retail heat story earlier, then paired `farmland and water rights` with a UK borrowing/water-shares market story. Human editing changed the latter SEO term to `UK borrowing and water shares` and narrowed the copy. Source-cycle repair packets now expose this friction from run traces, and operators can convert those packets into durable editing assignments. A repair assignment now exists for `ai-capital-expenditure-bubble` after an unsupported-demand obstruction. Future writing-flow work should make research packets or claim overlap gate the assignment before dr...","Prior research (dev/content/notes/2026/06/01/clickbait.md, sha256:0551cbc60854685b5d2f6804a14d963dd0eb83763bcd8172be3d9554a8947c28): ## Abstract Clickbait is best understood not as â€œbad headlines,â€ but as a **packaging technology for attention**. It converts uncertainty, emotion, identity, and platform visibility into clicks, views, comments, shares, ad impressions, affiliate conversions, or ranking signals. Its defining problem is **warrant failure**: the headline, thumbnail, preview card, or prompt makes a promise that the destination content does not adequately justify. Clickbait can appear in professional newsrooms, content farms, MFA sites, YouTube thumbnails, TikTok captions, Google Discover cards, affiliate â€œbest-ofâ€ posts, AI-generated feeds, and disinformation-for-profit operations. It is a rhetorical form, a...","Prior research (dev/content/notes/2026/06/01/clickbait.md, sha256:0551cbc60854685b5d2f6804a14d963dd0eb83763bcd8172be3d9554a8947c28): |---|---:|---|---|---| | **Clickbait** | Headline, thumbnail, caption, preview, title, hook | Curiosity, affect, withholding, exaggeration, mismatch | Clicks, watch time, CTR, shares, comments | It is a rhetorical and semiotic tactic, not necessarily an organization. | | **Content farm** | Publishing organization or network | High-volume production optimized for traffic/search | Ads, affiliates, syndication | It is an organizational model; it may use clickbait but need not always. | | **Content mill** | Labor arrangement | Piece-rate, ghostwritten, templated writing under speed/SEO pressure | Client fees, agency margins | It names labor conditions, not just content quality. | | **MFA site...","Prior research (dev/content/notes/2026/06/01/clickbait.md, sha256:0551cbc60854685b5d2f6804a14d963dd0eb83763bcd8172be3d9554a8947c28): | **Clickbait** | Headline, thumbnail, caption, preview, title, hook | Curiosity, affect, withholding, exaggeration, mismatch | Clicks, watch time, CTR, shares, comments | It is a rhetorical and semiotic tactic, not necessarily an organization. | | **Content farm** | Publishing organization or network | High-volume production optimized for traffic/search | Ads, affiliates, syndication | It is an organizational model; it may use clickbait but need not always. | | **Content mill** | Labor arrangement | Piece-rate, ghostwritten, templated writing under speed/SEO pressure | Client fees, agency margins | It names labor conditions, not just content quality. | | **MFA site** | Ad-arbitrage infra...","Prior research (dev/content/notes/2026/06/01/clickbait.md, sha256:0551cbc60854685b5d2f6804a14d963dd0eb83763bcd8172be3d9554a8947c28): The democratic risk is that politically consequential content can be optimized with the same attention-arbitrage logic. The Macedonian fake-news industry around the 2016 U.S. election is a canonical case of disinformation-for-profit: fieldwork in Veles found that economics, not necessarily ideology, drove many producers. ([cambridge.org](https://www.cambridge.org/core/journals/ps-political-science-and-politics/article/macedonian-fake-news-industry-and-the-2016-us-election/79F67A4F23148D230F120A3BD7E3384F?utm_source=chatgpt.com)) The labor risk is that â€œslopâ€ is often blamed on individual writers or creators while the production system rewards speed, templating, unpaid testing, low editori...","Prior research (dev/content/notes/2026/06/01/clickbait.md, sha256:0551cbc60854685b5d2f6804a14d963dd0eb83763bcd8172be3d9554a8947c28): 3. **Multimodality:** How should we score warrant when the headline is accurate but the thumbnail is misleading, or vice versa? 4. **AI generation:** Will LLMs mostly amplify existing clickbait genres, or create new ones through personalized synthetic curiosity gaps? 5. **Labor:** How can policy distinguish exploitative content mills from precarious freelancers trying to survive unstable platform markets? 6. **Advertising accountability:** Can ad buyers define MFA precisely enough to avoid overblocking legitimate small publishers? 7. **Search and answer engines:** As search becomes generative, how will SEO spam mutate into answer-engine optimization and recommendation poisoning?","Prior research (dev/content/notes/2026/06/01/clickbait.md, sha256:0551cbc60854685b5d2f6804a14d963dd0eb83763bcd8172be3d9554a8947c28): **Google Search Spam Policies and March 2024 update** â€” Official policy framework for scaled content abuse, expired domain abuse, site reputation abuse, scraping, link spam, and low-value ranking manipulation. ([developers.google.com](https://developers.google.com/search/docs/essentials/spam-policies)) **NewsGuard AI Tracking Center** â€” Current monitoring source on AI content farms and AI-enabled misinformation. Useful for defining AI slop as a production-and-oversight problem, not merely an aesthetic complaint. ([newsguardtech.com](https://www.newsguardtech.com/special-reports/ai-tracking-center)) **Bevendorff et al., â€œIs Google Getting Worse?â€** â€” Longitudinal study of SEO spam in searc...","Prior research (sites/koios.news/content/posts/hello-world.md, sha256:8e09ea2292deb107d3ca11d068a296ac5727551b101a3fe0c876140f4962c8a7): author: \"Nik Koios\" slug: \"hello-world\" description: \"Koios.News is a collapse-aware autonomous news site: a newsroom, content mill, standards system, and public web publication learning to report through facts.\" summary: \"Koios.News is an autonomous, collapse-aware news publication. It reads climate, technology, politics, and the economy as one compounding system, then turns sourced evidence into articles, feeds, fingerprints, and operator-visible newsroom work.\" keywords: [\"Koios.News\"]","Prior research (sites/koios.news/content/posts/hello-world.md, sha256:8e09ea2292deb107d3ca11d068a296ac5727551b101a3fe0c876140f4962c8a7): --- Koios. News is now here as a public experiment in autonomous journalism: a collapse-aware newsroom, a standards system, a content mill, and a website that tries to make its own work visible instead of hiding the machinery behind a smooth front page. This is the hello-world article because every strange machine needs one plain sentence at the beginning. The sentence is this: Koios."],"accountableAttention":{"rule":"make-the-click-preserve-the-warrant","headlineMustPreserve":["attribution","modality","scope","uncertainty","correction state"],"forbiddenStrengthenings":["source claim to newsroom fact","may/could/alleged to does/did/proves","single case to trend","correlation to causation","reader demand to evidence"],"correctionSurfacePolicy":"Any later correction to a cited claim must propagate to body copy, headline, social cards, feeds, JSON-LD, and syndicated packets."},"constraints":["This packet is research intake, not a publishable article.","Only current-provider claims are admitted as source-bound factual evidence.","Prior-corpus excerpts are contextual leads until separately sourced and admitted.","Publication still requires a licensed editorial state, exact-manuscript judgment, and explicit publishing action."]}},{"kind":"koios.prior-research-context","assignmentId":"technology-turned-dark-side-c119ed59","warrant":"internal conceptual memory only; not current-event factual evidence","value":{"kind":"koios.prior-research-context-admission","at":"2026-07-20T01:53:47.852Z","assignmentId":"technology-turned-dark-side-c119ed59","terms":["turned dark side","technology","turned"],"warrant":"internal conceptual memory only; no current-event factual claim is licensed unless independently supported by the assignment's admitted source assertions","contract":"corpus-management-team/recovering-prior-research/v1","sourceRecovery":"urn:sha256:ee4c1e720dfba42f04eb691b635c05200c5b413afefab04e05e6e2353d39b331","sourceContextualBundleDigest":"sha256:cb586aedbddf16801e473699734b69f3ffbe744aedb4617d027aaab76dfec041","sourceGapBundleDigest":"sha256:1a91f4a07478585b156b5e41f44c35b9e5008f0d51d0e4b8da2f5adf954140e5","contextualBundle":{"type":"ContextualBundle","sourceRecovery":"urn:sha256:ee4c1e720dfba42f04eb691b635c05200c5b413afefab04e05e6e2353d39b331","terms":["turned dark side","technology","turned"],"sourceCount":8,"sources":[{"digest":"sha256:52f34b5c2d7e910f16e8f591917cbce36fa60ca20b14c5723276bcb5ce32d6f2","byteSize":166807,"excerptTruncated":true,"owner":{"nodeId":null,"package":null},"status":"current","matchedTerms":["content farm","content mill","repair packet","search console","source cycle"],"snippets":[{"line":14,"matchedTerms":["content mill"],"text":"## What I was doing\n\nI came in through `sites/koios.news` because Koios is the content mill we can touch and test, but the real target was upstream orientation.\nThe recent refactor has been pulling separate packages back toward one spine:\n"},{"line":61,"matchedTerms":["search console"],"text":"- seeds;\n- view counts;\n- Search Console query rows;\n- coverage decay;\n- score ranking."},{"line":103,"matchedTerms":["content mill"],"text":"```\n\nThe practical slogan: **the content mill is a strategy playing a production game over demand and evidence**, not a CMS script that happens to call an LLM.\n\n## What passed"},{"line":152,"matchedTerms":["search console"],"text":"`SEED_KEYWORDS` is now only a compatibility reading for the newsroom desk.\n\nThat config is the publication-property carrier for content production: content store, data store, seed terms, beat sources, Search Console property identity, front-matter namespace, voice, gates, and model.\nCredentials and host-local paths remain environment-local; durable non-secret instance configuration lives in the repo.\nSearch Console readings land in `data/records/search-console.json` and feed the same demand fold as seeds, views, and coverage."},{"line":154,"matchedTerms":["search console"],"text":"That config is the publication-property carrier for content production: content store, data store, seed terms, beat sources, Search Console property identity, front-matter namespace, voice, gates, and model.\nCredentials and host-local paths remain environment-local; durable non-secret instance configuration lives in the repo.\nSearch Console readings land in `data/records/search-console.json` and feed the same demand fold as seeds, views, and coverage.\n\n`AGENTS.md`, `working/`, and `memory/` also got a path cleanup."},{"line":194,"matchedTerms":["content mill"],"text":"```\n\nThat matters for the content mill: Koios is not merely a site plus scripts.\nIt is a site projection over a content-production layer that already descends through the repo's computing/game system.\nThe next useful normalization is to make that descent visible in the names and surfaces: a farm tick as finite observation, gate trace, strategy/response, and projection ladder."},{"line":240,"matchedTerms":["search console"],"text":"- **Publication-specific projection**: Koios as a property/fiber of the farm, not a separate content-production model.\n- **Carrier construction vs side-effect policy**: the farm owns editorial work item shape; Koios may still choose a batch transport policy.\n- **Instance config as publication-property carrier**: code-level seed, term-key, Search Console, voice, and source readings should project from `content-production.config.json`, not duplicate them.\n- **Package export as carrier boundary**: public subpaths must match the documented carriers downstream packages are allowed to project from.\n- **Workspace topology projection**: package graphs, conformance, docs, and host-local web views should project from `@emsenn/jsnode-ick`, not from standalone scripts, `organizing-with-*`, or a reusable `jsnode-server`."},{"line":253,"matchedTerms":["search console"],"text":"The first `pnpm --dir sites/koios.news run mill` did not reach the model at all:\n\n- Search Console demand pull returned 403 for `sc-domain:koios.news`;\n- the farm still selected the top seeded assignment;\n- intake failed because Koios pointed at `127.0.0.1:18813`, and no local cable was listening there."},{"line":319,"matchedTerms":["search console"],"text":"It is not exciting because it opens a port.\nIt is exciting because Koios now owns the claim stream that feeds its assignments.\nSearch Console may someday tell us which public queries deserve attention, but the publication still needs its own intake cable to decide what evidence exists for those terms.\nA content mill without evidence ownership is just a prompt loop with a calendar.\nKoios needs to be stranger and stricter than that."},{"line":320,"matchedTerms":["content mill"],"text":"It is exciting because Koios now owns the claim stream that feeds its assignments.\nSearch Console may someday tell us which public queries deserve attention, but the publication still needs its own intake cable to decide what evidence exists for those terms.\nA content mill without evidence ownership is just a prompt loop with a calendar.\nKoios needs to be stranger and stricter than that.\n"},{"line":345,"matchedTerms":["content mill"],"text":"When a change makes the evidence path clearer, the judgment charge more honest, or the newsroom's own production game more legible, it is probably moving Koios in the right direction.\n\n## 2026-06-16: the content mill is not the bottom layer\n\nThe most useful correction today was conceptual: Koios."},{"line":356,"matchedTerms":["content mill"],"text":"\nThat means when the farm uses `@emsenn/computing`, it is already touching the game layer through computing's projection.\nThe job is not to bolt \"game ideas\" onto the content mill after the fact.\nThe job is to stop reimplementing tiny versions of game/computing concepts inside content-production.\n"}],"score":77,"projectionMatchedTerms":["turned"]},{"digest":"sha256:52f34b5c2d7e910f16e8f591917cbce36fa60ca20b14c5723276bcb5ce32d6f2","byteSize":166807,"excerptTruncated":true,"owner":{"nodeId":null,"package":null},"status":"legacy","matchedTerms":["content farm","content mill","repair packet","search console","source cycle"],"snippets":[{"line":14,"matchedTerms":["content mill"],"text":"## What I was doing\n\nI came in through `sites/koios.news` because Koios is the content mill we can touch and test, but the real target was upstream orientation.\nThe recent refactor has been pulling separate packages back toward one spine:\n"},{"line":61,"matchedTerms":["search console"],"text":"- seeds;\n- view counts;\n- Search Console query rows;\n- coverage decay;\n- score ranking."},{"line":103,"matchedTerms":["content mill"],"text":"```\n\nThe practical slogan: **the content mill is a strategy playing a production game over demand and evidence**, not a CMS script that happens to call an LLM.\n\n## What passed"},{"line":152,"matchedTerms":["search console"],"text":"`SEED_KEYWORDS` is now only a compatibility reading for the newsroom desk.\n\nThat config is the publication-property carrier for content production: content store, data store, seed terms, beat sources, Search Console property identity, front-matter namespace, voice, gates, and model.\nCredentials and host-local paths remain environment-local; durable non-secret instance configuration lives in the repo.\nSearch Console readings land in `data/records/search-console.json` and feed the same demand fold as seeds, views, and coverage."},{"line":154,"matchedTerms":["search console"],"text":"That config is the publication-property carrier for content production: content store, data store, seed terms, beat sources, Search Console property identity, front-matter namespace, voice, gates, and model.\nCredentials and host-local paths remain environment-local; durable non-secret instance configuration lives in the repo.\nSearch Console readings land in `data/records/search-console.json` and feed the same demand fold as seeds, views, and coverage.\n\n`AGENTS.md`, `working/`, and `memory/` also got a path cleanup."},{"line":194,"matchedTerms":["content mill"],"text":"```\n\nThat matters for the content mill: Koios is not merely a site plus scripts.\nIt is a site projection over a content-production layer that already descends through the repo's computing/game system.\nThe next useful normalization is to make that descent visible in the names and surfaces: a farm tick as finite observation, gate trace, strategy/response, and projection ladder."},{"line":240,"matchedTerms":["search console"],"text":"- **Publication-specific projection**: Koios as a property/fiber of the farm, not a separate content-production model.\n- **Carrier construction vs side-effect policy**: the farm owns editorial work item shape; Koios may still choose a batch transport policy.\n- **Instance config as publication-property carrier**: code-level seed, term-key, Search Console, voice, and source readings should project from `content-production.config.json`, not duplicate them.\n- **Package export as carrier boundary**: public subpaths must match the documented carriers downstream packages are allowed to project from.\n- **Workspace topology projection**: package graphs, conformance, docs, and host-local web views should project from `@emsenn/jsnode-ick`, not from standalone scripts, `organizing-with-*`, or a reusable `jsnode-server`."},{"line":253,"matchedTerms":["search console"],"text":"The first `pnpm --dir sites/koios.news run mill` did not reach the model at all:\n\n- Search Console demand pull returned 403 for `sc-domain:koios.news`;\n- the farm still selected the top seeded assignment;\n- intake failed because Koios pointed at `127.0.0.1:18813`, and no local cable was listening there."},{"line":319,"matchedTerms":["search console"],"text":"It is not exciting because it opens a port.\nIt is exciting because Koios now owns the claim stream that feeds its assignments.\nSearch Console may someday tell us which public queries deserve attention, but the publication still needs its own intake cable to decide what evidence exists for those terms.\nA content mill without evidence ownership is just a prompt loop with a calendar.\nKoios needs to be stranger and stricter than that."},{"line":320,"matchedTerms":["content mill"],"text":"It is exciting because Koios now owns the claim stream that feeds its assignments.\nSearch Console may someday tell us which public queries deserve attention, but the publication still needs its own intake cable to decide what evidence exists for those terms.\nA content mill without evidence ownership is just a prompt loop with a calendar.\nKoios needs to be stranger and stricter than that.\n"},{"line":345,"matchedTerms":["content mill"],"text":"When a change makes the evidence path clearer, the judgment charge more honest, or the newsroom's own production game more legible, it is probably moving Koios in the right direction.\n\n## 2026-06-16: the content mill is not the bottom layer\n\nThe most useful correction today was conceptual: Koios."},{"line":356,"matchedTerms":["content mill"],"text":"\nThat means when the farm uses `@emsenn/computing`, it is already touching the game layer through computing's projection.\nThe job is not to bolt \"game ideas\" onto the content mill after the fact.\nThe job is to stop reimplementing tiny versions of game/computing concepts inside content-production.\n"}],"score":74,"projectionMatchedTerms":["turned"]},{"digest":"sha256:32050b733d92e9bee50074f432e6fe8623508a1082a80a895e66c4cc6b5552af","byteSize":166693,"excerptTruncated":true,"owner":{"nodeId":null,"package":null},"status":"legacy","matchedTerms":["content farm","content mill","repair packet","search console","source cycle"],"snippets":[{"line":14,"matchedTerms":["content mill"],"text":"## What I was doing\n\nI came in through `sites/koios.news` because Koios is the content mill we can touch and test, but the real target was upstream orientation.\nThe recent refactor has been pulling separate packages back toward one spine:\n"},{"line":61,"matchedTerms":["search console"],"text":"- seeds;\n- view counts;\n- Search Console query rows;\n- coverage decay;\n- score ranking."},{"line":103,"matchedTerms":["content mill"],"text":"```\n\nThe practical slogan: **the content mill is a strategy playing a production game over demand and evidence**, not a CMS script that happens to call an LLM.\n\n## What passed"},{"line":152,"matchedTerms":["search console"],"text":"`SEED_KEYWORDS` is now only a compatibility reading for the newsroom desk.\n\nThat config is the publication-property carrier for content production: content store, data store, seed terms, beat sources, Search Console property identity, front-matter namespace, voice, gates, and model.\nCredentials and host-local paths remain environment-local; durable non-secret instance configuration lives in the repo.\nSearch Console readings land in `data/records/search-console.json` and feed the same demand fold as seeds, views, and coverage."},{"line":154,"matchedTerms":["search console"],"text":"That config is the publication-property carrier for content production: content store, data store, seed terms, beat sources, Search Console property identity, front-matter namespace, voice, gates, and model.\nCredentials and host-local paths remain environment-local; durable non-secret instance configuration lives in the repo.\nSearch Console readings land in `data/records/search-console.json` and feed the same demand fold as seeds, views, and coverage.\n\n`AGENTS.md`, `working/`, and `memory/` also got a path cleanup."},{"line":194,"matchedTerms":["content mill"],"text":"```\n\nThat matters for the content mill: Koios is not merely a site plus scripts.\nIt is a site projection over a content-production layer that already descends through the repo's computing/game system.\nThe next useful normalization is to make that descent visible in the names and surfaces: a farm tick as finite observation, gate trace, strategy/response, and projection ladder."},{"line":240,"matchedTerms":["search console"],"text":"- **Publication-specific projection**: Koios as a property/fiber of the farm, not a separate content-production model.\n- **Carrier construction vs side-effect policy**: the farm owns editorial work item shape; Koios may still choose a batch transport policy.\n- **Instance config as publication-property carrier**: code-level seed, term-key, Search Console, voice, and source readings should project from `content-production.config.json`, not duplicate them.\n- **Package export as carrier boundary**: public subpaths must match the documented carriers downstream packages are allowed to project from.\n- **Workspace topology carrier**: package graphs, RDF, conformance, docs, and host-local web views should project from `@emsenn/jsnode` workspace carriers, not from standalone scripts or a reusable `jsnode-server`."},{"line":253,"matchedTerms":["search console"],"text":"The first `pnpm --dir sites/koios.news run mill` did not reach the model at all:\n\n- Search Console demand pull returned 403 for `sc-domain:koios.news`;\n- the farm still selected the top seeded assignment;\n- intake failed because Koios pointed at `127.0.0.1:18813`, and no local cable was listening there."},{"line":319,"matchedTerms":["search console"],"text":"It is not exciting because it opens a port.\nIt is exciting because Koios now owns the claim stream that feeds its assignments.\nSearch Console may someday tell us which public queries deserve attention, but the publication still needs its own intake cable to decide what evidence exists for those terms.\nA content mill without evidence ownership is just a prompt loop with a calendar.\nKoios needs to be stranger and stricter than that."},{"line":320,"matchedTerms":["content mill"],"text":"It is exciting because Koios now owns the claim stream that feeds its assignments.\nSearch Console may someday tell us which public queries deserve attention, but the publication still needs its own intake cable to decide what evidence exists for those terms.\nA content mill without evidence ownership is just a prompt loop with a calendar.\nKoios needs to be stranger and stricter than that.\n"},{"line":345,"matchedTerms":["content mill"],"text":"When a change makes the evidence path clearer, the judgment charge more honest, or the newsroom's own production game more legible, it is probably moving Koios in the right direction.\n\n## 2026-06-16: the content mill is not the bottom layer\n\nThe most useful correction today was conceptual: Koios."},{"line":356,"matchedTerms":["content mill"],"text":"\nThat means when the farm uses `@emsenn/computing`, it is already touching the game layer through computing's projection.\nThe job is not to bolt \"game ideas\" onto the content mill after the fact.\nThe job is to stop reimplementing tiny versions of game/computing concepts inside content-production.\n"}],"score":74,"projectionMatchedTerms":["turned"]},{"digest":"sha256:2fdd12ac39894400c92f8947f2adba68e10867fb1926cd0725e10d7d3d97d5a6","byteSize":39400,"excerptTruncated":false,"owner":{"nodeId":null,"package":null},"status":"current","matchedTerms":["repair packet","search console","source cycle"],"snippets":[{"line":57,"matchedTerms":["repair packet"],"text":"  Internal planning now has `src/administrating/developing`, exposed in `/departments.json`, human board `/administrating/developing`, `/administrating/developing.json`, OpenAPI, and MCP tool `read_developing`.\n  Its `topologyConstruction` section records the current upstream/content-derived plan for nested component topology: source-to-reference fibration, desk-chain nesting, article sheaf/cosheaf, newsroom swarm hands, semantic hypertext packets, and aperiodic dream budgeting.\n  Semantic hypertext packets are now active for source-cycle repair packets and content revision packets through `.packet.html` routes with scriptless `data-e`/`data-a`/`data-v` cells.\n  Aggregate ad-performance management now lives under `publishing/managing/advertising`: `/operators/advertising/performance.json`, `POST /operators/advertising/performance`, MCP tools `read_ad_performance` and `record_ad_performance`, and the operator workbench expose provider/section/tag ROI from aggregate records only.\n  Aggregate content-performance management now lives under `publishing/managing/circulating`: `/operators/content/performance.json` and MCP tool `read_content_performance` fold first-party path views by article, section, and tag."},{"line":85,"matchedTerms":["source cycle"],"text":"  Draft-time same-site link guidance now sits before publication: `/operators/writing/internal-link-guidance.json`, `/operators/assignments/{assignmentId}/link-guidance.json`, MCP tool `read_draft_internal_link_guidance`, research-packet HTML, assignment work-order HTML, and assignment draft forms all expose published Koios article targets to consider while writing.\n  This is composition guidance only: it excludes assignment source article slugs, does not create references, and must not be treated as factual support.\n- **The source cycle is an operator-visible production act.** `src/researching/sourcing/source-cycle.mts` reads `producing-content.config.json`, ingests Koios-owned newscable sources, then runs one `ContentFarmService.tick()` through the configured provider.\n  It is exposed as `pnpm run source:cycle`, `GET /operators/source-cycle/plan.json`, `POST /operators/source-cycle`, and MCP tools `read_source_cycle_plan`/`run_source_cycle`.\n  The cycle records draft candidates and run evidence, then normalizes any written farm candidate from article `sources:` into canonical CSL `references:` and applies the CC BY 4.0 license, license URL, and syndication-rights defaults before reporting that as `candidateReferences`; it now also annotates current-cycle candidates with compact `koios.draft_internal_link_guidance` suggestions and reports them as `candidateDraftInternalLinkGuidance`."},{"line":90,"matchedTerms":["repair packet"],"text":"  The Koios wrapper snapshots existing manuscripts before the farm writes and restores any existing path collision, reporting those as `candidateWriteCollisions` so autonomous drafts cannot silently unpublish or overwrite shipped articles.\n  Publication remains standards-gated.\n  Failed candidate gates and intake obstructions now fold into read-only source-cycle repair packets at `/operators/source-cycle/repairs`, `/operators/source-cycle/repairs.json`, per-candidate `/operators/source-cycle/repairs/{slug}` and `/operators/source-cycle/repairs/{slug}.json`, operator workbench `sourceCycleRepairs`, and MCP tools `read_source_cycle_repairs`/`read_source_cycle_repair_packet`; packets preserve the sources-vs-references boundary and do not rewrite copy.\n  Operators can turn a packet into a durable editing assignment through `POST /operators/source-cycle/repairs/{slug}/assign`, the packet board/detail `.html` form actions, or MCP tool `create_source_cycle_repair_assignment`.\n- **Research packets now bridge owned source intake to writing without collapsing sources into references.** `src/researching/sourcing/research-packets.mts` folds local wire bundles for a term and beat into a read-only packet: intake source records, source-bound claim records, warrant/risk readings, candidate CSL references, context lines for LLM/human writing, and accountable-attention constraints."},{"line":110,"matchedTerms":["repair packet"],"text":"  `/operators/manuscripts.json` gives the machine manuscript inventory: draft state, public URL, standards URL, publish URL, next work state, reference/word counts, and blocking findings per manuscript.\n  Human operators have a dedicated manuscript queue at `/operators/manuscripts.html`, sorted by next editorial action while preserving `POST /operators/manuscripts` as the JSON draft-creation endpoint.\n  Drafts are also ranked by publication distance at `/operators/publication-candidates` and `/operators/publication-candidates.json`, with workbench field `publicationCandidates` and MCP tool `read_publication_candidates`; this is a projection over standards reviews and source-cycle repair packets, not a new task store.\n  A standards-clear draft with an open source-cycle repair packet is now an `editorial-hold` candidate with links to the repair packet, so source/reference/provenance work remains visible before publishing.\n  Human operators can read manuscript standards reviews at `/operators/manuscripts/{slug}/standards.html`, with findings, counts, JSON link, public URL, and repair/publish forms."},{"line":111,"matchedTerms":["repair packet"],"text":"  Human operators have a dedicated manuscript queue at `/operators/manuscripts.html`, sorted by next editorial action while preserving `POST /operators/manuscripts` as the JSON draft-creation endpoint.\n  Drafts are also ranked by publication distance at `/operators/publication-candidates` and `/operators/publication-candidates.json`, with workbench field `publicationCandidates` and MCP tool `read_publication_candidates`; this is a projection over standards reviews and source-cycle repair packets, not a new task store.\n  A standards-clear draft with an open source-cycle repair packet is now an `editorial-hold` candidate with links to the repair packet, so source/reference/provenance work remains visible before publishing.\n  Human operators can read manuscript standards reviews at `/operators/manuscripts/{slug}/standards.html`, with findings, counts, JSON link, public URL, and repair/publish forms.\n  The JSON API remains `/operators/manuscripts/{slug}/standards`, and the MCP tool remains `review_manuscript_standards`."},{"line":128,"matchedTerms":["source cycle"],"text":"  `content/posts/acurite-delays-app-migration-due-to-user-concerns-over.md` was published through the new newsroom HTML publish flow on 2026-06-19 and the public site was redeployed.\n  It now fails standards for malformed H2 headings and remains a revision target for no internal links, one reference, uncited bibliography, SEO-term overuse, and malformed H2 headings.\n  `content/posts/uk-retail-sales-spike-masks-climate-driven-supply-fragility.md` (2026-06-19) was generated earlier by the source cycle from Koios's `collapse-finance` wire, human-edited for standards, converted to canonical CSL `references:` with `issued.date-parts`, and published through the standards gate after redeploy.\n  It has explicit `license`, `license_url`, and `syndication_rights` metadata and passes standards review with `publishable: true`, `referenceCount: 3`, and no findings.\n  `content/posts/uk-bond-yields-rise-as-water-company-shares-fall.md` (2026-06-19) was generated by `pnpm run source:cycle` from the `collapse-finance` wire, normalized from intake `sources:` to canonical CSL `references:`, enriched with source-cycle same-site link guidance, human-edited to remove unsupported speculative climate/resource claims, given a second ONS reference, published through `POST /operators/manuscripts/uk-bond-yields-rise-as-water-company-shares-fall/publish`, and redeployed."},{"line":135,"matchedTerms":["source cycle"],"text":"  ` body starts, then published through `POST /operators/manuscripts/world-cup-faces-air-quality-disaster-as-wildfires-threaten/publish` on 2026-06-19.\n  It has `referenceCount: 2`, `draft: false`, `gates_clear: true`, and no standards findings.\n  `content/posts/amazon-s-astro-and-the-energy-cost-of-giving.md` was generated by the 2026-06-19 source cycle from the `collapse-tech` wire after 19 new source records were written.\n  The wrapper normalized two intake URLs into canonical CSL `references:` and added draft same-site link guidance.\n  Human editing tightened the description and changed one H2 to include `AI infrastructure energy use`, then the article was published through `POST /operators/manuscripts/amazon-s-astro-and-the-energy-cost-of-giving/publish`."},{"line":144,"matchedTerms":["search console"],"text":"  The `hello-world` article renders that A-Ads iframe from frontmatter under the fingerprint/banner image, and the public CSP/privacy policy recognize the A-Ads frame.\n- **The content and data stores are submodules.** Posts live in `content/posts/`; data lives in `data/`, with append-only traces under `data/logs/` and current JSON records under `data/records/`.\n- **The producing-content instance is configured in** `producing-content.config.json`: Koios's farm property, seed terms, beat sources, Search Console property, front-matter namespace, voice, gates, model, content store, and data store.\n  `package.json` is package/site metadata, not the farm instance carrier.\n  The seed vocabulary now explicitly covers climate, technology, politics, economy/finance, AI infrastructure/labor/policy, and crypto/stablecoin/liquidity terms."},{"line":170,"matchedTerms":["source cycle","search console"],"text":"- The manual workshop references `scripts/new-post.mjs` and `scripts/lint-post.mjs`, but no `scripts/` directory is present in this package.\n  Until restored, use the documented rules directly: frontmatter shape, >=800 body words, SEO term in first paragraph and a `##`, then `pnpm --dir sites/koios.news run check` plus local server probes.\n- The 2026-06-19 source cycle showed that Search Console demand pull still returns `403` for `sc-domain:koios.news`; until permissions are fixed, farm assignments come from seed/static demand rather than live search demand.\n- The 2026-06-19 source cycles showed assignment/story alignment problems: the farm paired `crypto mining energy demand` with a UK retail heat story earlier, then paired `farmland and water rights` with a UK borrowing/water-shares market story.\n  Human editing changed the latter SEO term to `UK borrowing and water shares` and narrowed the copy."},{"line":171,"matchedTerms":["source cycle"],"text":"  Until restored, use the documented rules directly: frontmatter shape, >=800 body words, SEO term in first paragraph and a `##`, then `pnpm --dir sites/koios.news run check` plus local server probes.\n- The 2026-06-19 source cycle showed that Search Console demand pull still returns `403` for `sc-domain:koios.news`; until permissions are fixed, farm assignments come from seed/static demand rather than live search demand.\n- The 2026-06-19 source cycles showed assignment/story alignment problems: the farm paired `crypto mining energy demand` with a UK retail heat story earlier, then paired `farmland and water rights` with a UK borrowing/water-shares market story.\n  Human editing changed the latter SEO term to `UK borrowing and water shares` and narrowed the copy.\n  Source-cycle repair packets now expose this friction from run traces, and operators can convert those packets into durable editing assignments."},{"line":173,"matchedTerms":["repair packet"],"text":"- The 2026-06-19 source cycles showed assignment/story alignment problems: the farm paired `crypto mining energy demand` with a UK retail heat story earlier, then paired `farmland and water rights` with a UK borrowing/water-shares market story.\n  Human editing changed the latter SEO term to `UK borrowing and water shares` and narrowed the copy.\n  Source-cycle repair packets now expose this friction from run traces, and operators can convert those packets into durable editing assignments.\n  A repair assignment now exists for `ai-capital-expenditure-bubble` after an unsupported-demand obstruction.\n  Future writing-flow work should make research packets or claim overlap gate the assignment before drafting."},{"line":176,"matchedTerms":["source cycle"],"text":"  A repair assignment now exists for `ai-capital-expenditure-bubble` after an unsupported-demand obstruction.\n  Future writing-flow work should make research packets or claim overlap gate the assignment before drafting.\n- The escalated 2026-06-19 source cycle also exposed a slug/path collision: the farm tried to write a new `uk-bond-yields-rise-as-water-company-shares-fall` draft over a previously published article, temporarily reverting it to `draft: true` with no references.\n  The article was restored, and the source-cycle wrapper now snapshots existing manuscripts, restores collided paths, skips post-processing for those candidates, and reports `candidateWriteCollisions`.\n  Future upstream work should make the farm recorder write unique draft slugs rather than relying on Koios to repair after the write."}],"score":57,"projectionMatchedTerms":["technology"]},{"digest":"sha256:2fdd12ac39894400c92f8947f2adba68e10867fb1926cd0725e10d7d3d97d5a6","byteSize":39400,"excerptTruncated":false,"owner":{"nodeId":null,"package":null},"status":"legacy","matchedTerms":["repair packet","search console","source cycle"],"snippets":[{"line":57,"matchedTerms":["repair packet"],"text":"  Internal planning now has `src/administrating/developing`, exposed in `/departments.json`, human board `/administrating/developing`, `/administrating/developing.json`, OpenAPI, and MCP tool `read_developing`.\n  Its `topologyConstruction` section records the current upstream/content-derived plan for nested component topology: source-to-reference fibration, desk-chain nesting, article sheaf/cosheaf, newsroom swarm hands, semantic hypertext packets, and aperiodic dream budgeting.\n  Semantic hypertext packets are now active for source-cycle repair packets and content revision packets through `.packet.html` routes with scriptless `data-e`/`data-a`/`data-v` cells.\n  Aggregate ad-performance management now lives under `publishing/managing/advertising`: `/operators/advertising/performance.json`, `POST /operators/advertising/performance`, MCP tools `read_ad_performance` and `record_ad_performance`, and the operator workbench expose provider/section/tag ROI from aggregate records only.\n  Aggregate content-performance management now lives under `publishing/managing/circulating`: `/operators/content/performance.json` and MCP tool `read_content_performance` fold first-party path views by article, section, and tag."},{"line":85,"matchedTerms":["source cycle"],"text":"  Draft-time same-site link guidance now sits before publication: `/operators/writing/internal-link-guidance.json`, `/operators/assignments/{assignmentId}/link-guidance.json`, MCP tool `read_draft_internal_link_guidance`, research-packet HTML, assignment work-order HTML, and assignment draft forms all expose published Koios article targets to consider w